# Ignore test output directory
tests/test-output/
# Test-performance history (performance.json snapshots appended by `make wrelease`).
# Local to veda; charts are generated from this file, never from git history.
tests/perf-history/
# Runtime performance data — accumulates between releases
docs/performance/current/
# ADR 100 D8: the release baseline (run_*.json + runtime-performance-history.csv)
# lives on veda only. Veda is the one host that generates performance reports;
# `make wrelease` still promotes current/ into it, it just never commits it.
docs/performance/release/
# Ignore Python bytecode cache directories and compiled files
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.cache
*.cache.write
untrack_todo.md
to_be_added/
FUTURE/
wingman.log
wingman_live.log
*.log
# ADR 012: session recording videos and BT trace files — large/per-run debug
# artifacts, never meant to be published (see logs/session_*.mp4, logs/bt_trace_*.jsonl)
logs/session_*.mp4
logs/bt_trace_*.jsonl
# ADR 100 D7: the whole corpus (including telemetry/, integration_test/, and
# the loose top-level PNGs D5 originally kept tracked) lives on veda only now.
# `git rm --cached` was needed once to untrack what this line alone cannot
# touch — see D1's identical lesson about already-tracked paths.
test_screenshots/*
test_screenshots/*focus-probe.log
test_screenshots/health_dropouts/*
test_screenshots/unknown_anomalies/*
# ADR 100 D1: generated runtime trend charts. 4.6 MB each, rebuilt wholesale on
# every release, so consecutive versions barely delta — 77 blobs / 357 MB of
# history for two paths. Regenerate with `make runtime-perf-release`.
docs/performance/runtime-performance-trends.html
docs/performance/runtime-performance-trends.preview.html
# Per-user Claude Code permissions — personal, never shared
.claude/settings.local.json
